 ## Overview
-This method improves the 3D reconstruction of repetitive objects by creating a single shared Gaussian representation for all instances of the same object type. It allows information propagation, such as geometry completion and detail propagation, across instances while handling appearance differences via per-instance offsets. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting where each instance is independent, this method shares geometry parameters across instances, improving reconstruction quality for occluded or low-quality regions by leveraging multi-view information from all instances.
+This method improves the 3D reconstruction of repetitive objects by creating a single shared Gaussian representation for all instances of the same object type [S1]. It allows information propagation, such as geometry completion and detail propagation, across instances while handling appearance differences via per-instance offsets [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting where each instance is independent, this method shares geometry parameters across instances, improving reconstruction quality for occluded or low-quality regions by leveraging multi-view information from all instances [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Inputs:** A set of input images, initial camera poses, and an initial set of 3D Gaussians for each instance. The method assumes instances of the same object type have been identified.
-*   **Outputs:** A shared set of 3D Gaussian parameters (position, scale, rotation, opacity, shared SH coefficients) and per-instance parameters (rigid transformation, SH offset coefficients).
+*   **Inputs:** Initial camera poses, an initial set of 3D Gaussians for each instance, and a pre-identification of instances belonging to the same object type [S1].
+*   **Outputs:** A shared set of 3D Gaussian parameters (position, scale, rotation, opacity, shared SH coefficients) and per-instance parameters (rigid transformation, SH offset coefficients) [S1].
 
